---
import { bounds, story } from "../../lib/coverage";
import { noScore, pipeline, rileyAsk, spell, toPlay } from "../../lib/cases";

const record = [
  ["Schedule pages", `${pipeline.asked} expected, ${pipeline.saved} saved. Dunmore: unavailable, no answer after three tries.`],
  ["Matches", `${story.scheduled} scheduled by the format, ${toPlay} still to play, ${story.finals} finished.`],
  ["Read", `${story.counted} from the hosts' pages. ${spell(bounds.unseen, true)} Dunmore home matches from the visitors' saved pages.`],
  ["Not counted", `${noScore.home} vs. ${noScore.away}, ${noScore.day}: final, no score on either schedule. Box score page not requested yet.`],
];
---

<section id="rewind">
  <h2>Rewind: the same Friday, prompted properly</h2>
  <p>Here is Riley's original prompt again:</p>
  <div class="cv-user-prompt" role="region" aria-label="Riley's original prompt">
    <div class="cv-chat-bar">
      <span class="cv-chat-badge">Prompt</span>
      <span class="cv-chat-meta">Riley → Kick</span>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-chat-text">{rileyAsk}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cv-commit" data-commit>
    <label class="cv-write" for="cv-added">Add the one sentence that was missing.</label>
    <textarea id="cv-added" rows="2" placeholder="What would you require Kick to report?" data-save="added"></textarea>
    <div class="cv-actions">
      <button type="button" data-commit-btn disabled>Compare and replay Friday</button>
      <button type="button" class="cv-link-btn" data-commit-skip>Skip and show example</button>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write a short sentence to compare, or skip ahead.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <p class="cv-model">Before you collect, list every page and match the table should include, and in your summary report what happened to each, naming every gap.</p>
      <fieldset class="cv-ticks">
        <legend>Check what yours covers:</legend>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="added-set" /><span>Lists what should be collected before the run starts</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="added-each" /><span>Reports what happened to each expected item</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="added-gaps" /><span>Requires the summary to name every gap</span></label>
      </fieldset>

      <h3>What Kick returns when asked</h3>
      <p class="cv-label">Simulated response. Same agent, same Dunmore outage.</p>
      <table class="cv-log cv-record">
        <caption>Kick's coverage record, Friday</caption>
        <tbody>{record.map(([what, said]) => <tr><th scope="row">{what}</th><td>{said}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="cv-say">
        <p class="cv-who">Riley, to the eight schools <span>Monday morning</span></p>
        <p>Corrected table attached. It counts {story.afterRepair} of {story.finals} finished conference matches. Dunmore's page did not answer on Friday, so its {spell(bounds.unseen)} home results come from the visitors' pages. Hartwell Tech is second. {noScore.home} vs. {noScore.away} on {noScore.day} is final with no score on either schedule. Its box score page has not been checked yet, so both schools are one match short.</p>
      </div>
      <p>The outage didn't disappear. {spell(bounds.unseen, true)} results were recovered from saved pages, one stayed unknown and named, and the table went out as {story.afterRepair} of {story.finals}. Same AI agent, same outage; the difference was knowing what to require.</p>
      <p data-close-first hidden>Your question from Publish Day: <q></q> Would its answer have surfaced Dunmore's missing page?</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cv-next">Next: apply the same thinking to a season where nobody called to complain.</p>
</section>
